00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:05.460
When creating documents within Word,
there may be occasions where you

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.550
wish to include some interactive
element within the document, such

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.530
as check boxes or dropdown lists.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.190
To do this, you would need
to use the tools that are

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.540
featured on the developer tab.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.340
So if you look at the top of your tool
bar, if the developer tab isn't available,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.200
you would first need to activate it.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.150
To do that, if you go along to the
Word menu and select preferences

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.670
and then ribbon and toolbar.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.970
And on the ribbon and toolbar on
the right-hand side, you can see

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.280
that the main tabs are all ticked.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.870
If the developer tab isn't ticked, you
would just need to tick that select save.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.510
And then that will
activate the developer tab.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.769
So once you're on the developer
tab, you'll see a range of tools

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.040
that can be used to add various
functionality to the document.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.180
The two that we're going to focus
on are check boxes, and combo box.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.590
So for this first letter, I'm just
going to add some simple check boxes.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.550
What I need to do is place my cursor
to the right of the first option.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.970
And I'm going to use a tab key to line
them up just a little bit further away.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.950
And then I'm going to click the checkbox
icon, which will then insert a check box.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.030
I will repeat that for
the next five options.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.540
So move it down, tab key.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:25.830
Add the checkbox, use the tab key
checkbox, again a tab key to line

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:30.960
them up and finally the last checkbox.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.310
So now I have all the check boxes
inserted and they're all lined up

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.440
and now need to make them active.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.200
And to do that, I need to
click on the protect form.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:44.330
Once you've clicked on the protect
form button you can then select or

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.210
deselect the check boxes as required.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.140
I can't edit any of the
rest of the document.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.970
However anyone could unprotect
the form and then make changes.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.089
To protect the document fully, you would
need to add a password and to do that

00:02:01.089 --> 00:02:03.690
you would need to go to the tools menu.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:08.310
From tools you would select
protect document that will then

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.660
allow you to add a password.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.040
And the protection you're looking
for is to protect the document for

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:20.220
forms, add the password, select OK.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.810
It will ask you to repeat
the password, select OK.

00:02:26.805 --> 00:02:28.275
And that is now set.

00:02:28.305 --> 00:02:33.165
So once the document has been
protected with a password by clicking

00:02:33.165 --> 00:02:37.215
on that you would need to enter a
password to unprotect the document.

00:02:40.705 --> 00:02:43.340
As well as adding check boxes,
there may be occasions where

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.899
you wish to add a dropdown box.

00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:48.410
So as you can see, I've slightly
edited the letter that I was working

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.359
with and reduced some of the options.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.340
I'm now going to add some dropdown
lists, which will indicate a specific

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.820
number and then the reader can then
select that number to say which

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.380
experience that they're interested in.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.320
So again, I'm on the developer
tab and what I need to do, is

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.130
I'm going to add a combo box.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:11.849
So I'm going to use the tab key
to space the dropdown list away

00:03:11.899 --> 00:03:16.709
from the option, select a combo
box and then click on options.

00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:21.570
Now it's basically asking me what I
want to include in the dropdown list.

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:24.359
So the first thing I'm
going to add some numbers.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.499
So I click one and add that.

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:35.220
Two add that, three,
four, and finally five.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.829
Add that.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.720
So we now have all of the options
I want in the dropdown list, and

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.160
I'm just going to edit the name.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.740
So it's just dropdown one, remove the
hyphen from there and click OK and that

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.440
will have added the drop-down list.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.380
So if I click on that.,
nothing happens again.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.700
You have to protect the form.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.730
So once it's protected, I can then
make selections from the dropdown list.

00:04:04.245 --> 00:04:06.165
I'll just unprotect the form again.

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:10.185
Now to repeat that for the next two
options, I would go again to the

00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:15.315
combo box, do the options and add
the five numbers or whatever else

00:04:15.315 --> 00:04:16.995
I wanted to add the dropdown box.

00:04:17.355 --> 00:04:20.805
Alternatively, because I know that the
dropdown box is going to be the same

00:04:20.805 --> 00:04:22.545
for both of the other experiences.

00:04:22.605 --> 00:04:28.335
I can just highlight that and
use the Command and C to copy it

00:04:28.575 --> 00:04:30.305
and go down to the next option.

00:04:30.865 --> 00:04:37.724
Use Command and V and again for that
one Command and V and then if I protect

00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:46.034
the form, I have now added the dropdown
lists to all three of the options.

00:04:47.115 --> 00:04:50.924
As with the forms, if you wish to protect
it with a password, you would need to

00:04:50.924 --> 00:04:56.385
go to the tools menu, and then select
protect document and add a password.

